From: p5r-proton
Subject: ntdll: restore Wine 7 critical section debug info default

Wine 7 allocated RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_DEBUG for every critical section unless
the caller explicitly passed RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_NO_DEBUG_INFO. Wine 8.11
commit 8b3944e1341 ("ntdll: Only allocate debug info in critical sections with
RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_FORCE_DEBUG_INFO") inverted that default.

The change is not just bookkeeping. With debug info, Wine waits on the
LockSemaphore word with RtlWaitOnAddress() and wakes one waiter with
RtlWakeAddressSingle(). Without debug info, the CS uses a lazily created real
semaphore; NtReleaseSemaphore() reaches fsync_release_semaphore(), which does
futex_wake(..., INT_MAX) and wakes every waiter. P5R's four update threads all
contend on the same short-lived sections, so modern Wine wakes all four on
every release while Wine 7 woke exactly one. The three losers immediately fail
the LockSemaphore CAS and go back to the futex, which matches the observed
~0.9 CPU correlation and ~27% system time across those four threads.

Restore the Wine 7 default so normal critical sections keep the single-waiter
futex path.
--- a/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
@@ -227,7 +227,14 @@
      * is done, then debug info should be managed through Rtlp[Allocate|Free]DebugInfo
      * so (e.g.) MakeCriticalSectionGlobal() doesn't free it using HeapFree().
      */
-    if (!(flags & RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_FORCE_DEBUG_INFO))
+    /* Wine 7 allocated debug info for every critical section unless the caller
+     * explicitly passed RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_NO_DEBUG_INFO. That selects
+     * the single-waiter RtlWakeAddressSingle() path in
+     * RtlpUnWaitCriticalSection(). Wine 11 instead defaults normal sections to
+     * no debug info, so they wait on a real semaphore and NtReleaseSemaphore()
+     * wakes every fsync waiter, which turns P5R's four update threads into a
+     * thundering herd. Restore the Wine 7 default. */
+    if (flags & RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_NO_DEBUG_INFO)
         crit->DebugInfo = no_debug_info_marker;
     else
     {
